  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe `camcraft-ui` lib tests that make a wgpu instance now use the GPU one at a time. The change is in test code only.\n\n- New test-only module `crates/ui/src/egui_app/gpu_test_lock.rs` (`#[cfg(test)]`). It holds one process-wide `Mutex<()>` and the function `gpu_guard()`.\n- The lock is poison-tolerant. A test that panics with the lock held does not make the other GPU tests fail.\n- A holder counter fails a test if two tests hold the lock at the same time.\n- Eight tests take the guard as their first statement:\n  - `egui_app::tests::headless_run_succeeds`\n  - `egui_app::gpu::tests::adapter_probe_names_the_gpu`\n  - six `egui_app::report_tests` tests that push a kind button. The screenshot request makes `egui_kittest` start its wgpu renderer in `step()`.\n- The guard comes before the harness. Thus the harness and its renderer drop first, and the lock is released last.\n- The context pack named seven tests. `the_door_opens_the_window_and_a_kind_button_files_the_url` also pushes a kind button (\"Request a feature\"), so it takes the lock too.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3589-gpu-test-lock.md`. A shared instance was dropped: kittest makes its own device, and the headless run makes its device through `camcraft_gpu::device()`.\n\n## Product path\n\nThe product does not make two wgpu instances or devices at the same time. This is from a read of the code (scout pack on main 60376ccbb), not from a run:\n\n- The desktop app makes one instance, one adapter and one device on the UI thread (`gpu_init.rs`). It tries the backends in sequence. It drops each failed attempt before the next one.\n- The `--headless` run makes one instance on the calling thread (`crates/gpu/src/adapter.rs`).\n- `shared_device()` and `cut_or_cpu` have no caller outside `camcraft-gpu`.\n- No worker thread touches a device.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::gpu_test_lock::every_gpu_test_takes_the_lock`: reads the source of the eight tests. It requires `let _gpu = gpu_guard()` as the first statement of each.\n- `egui_app::gpu_test_lock::the_lock_lets_one_holder_in_at_a_time`: 8 threads take the lock 20 times each. The counter must never be more than 1.\n- `egui_app::gpu_test_lock::a_panic_with_the_lock_held_does_not_block_the_next_test`\n\nA test cannot prove that a random driver crash does not occur again. The proof is the repeat runs of the reporter on the affected machine.\n\n## Readings (this machine, Windows 11, `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -j 6`)\n\n- Run 1: ok. 1484 passed; 0 failed; 8 ignored (88.66 s). No 0xc0000005.\n- Run 2: ok. 1484 passed; 0 failed; 8 ignored (88.88 s). No 0xc0000005.\n- Run 3: ok. 1484 passed; 0 failed; 8 ignored (89.94 s). No 0xc0000005.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -j 6 -- -D warnings`: clean. The only warning is the old manifest warning about the unused workspace dependency `truck-polymesh`.\n- The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by 3. There is no snapshot PNG change and no new dependency.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- This machine did not show the crash before the change. The 20 runs on the reporter's machine are the test.\n- No heavy lane was run: this is a P2 PR with test code only.\n- The integration test binaries of `crates/ui` (`gpu_render`, `trace_*`, `catalog_render`) are separate processes and are not changed.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #3589\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
